        "notes": "Read both proof steps and all nine direct supplier statements. Infinite exponential-series radius and continuity make t maps to exp(-t) Borel; composition with the measurable energy supplies a positive measurable density. The density-measure definition and its proved well-definedness supplier give countable additivity; multiplication by the positive finite constant Z inverse commutes with the nonnegative partial-sum limit. Total mass is exactly one. The argument neither assumes sigma-finiteness nor requires choices; empty X, zero measure, Z=0 and Z=infinity are excluded by admissibility, and Z=1 is valid. Definition and Statement references remain uninterrupted. No defect or repair."
