          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "**Bounded-bilinear product rule.** If $f : U \\to Y$ and $g : U \\to Z$ are Fréchet differentiable at $x$, and $B : Y \\times Z \\to W$ is bounded bilinear, then $U \\ni u \\mapsto B(f(u),g(u))$ is Fréchet differentiable at $x$ and $$D\\bigl(B(f,g)\\bigr)(x)h = B\\bigl(Df(x)h,\\ g(x)\\bigr) + B\\bigl(f(x),\\ Dg(x)h\\bigr) \\qquad (h \\in X).$$",
