        "notes": "Read every current step and all 27 direct supplier statements, and compared complete hash-bound pre-reader and reader-post archives. The current item exactly equals reader-post raw SHA256 9d62afde61a7659100e735c1b4974ccc5f012183ef48e0e125581fe6492edcdd; recovered preimage exactly matches pre raw SHA256 58a593c3ec2907528aeaecfcafd103ffd11c42a57580187a4418b7c5445b140d. Statement and original claim strength are unchanged. The old proof already described mollification but left its supporting results undeclared; reader supplies and verifies those interfaces. Step 1.1 normalizes a nonnegative bump with explicit positive finite box bounds and derives its gradient bound. Step 2.1 applies convolution smoothing to a locally integrable compact C1 test, differentiates it under an explicit integrable majorant, and uses common compact support with local integrability to pass smooth weak identities by dominated convergence. Only the finite diagonal sum is taken before the global limit, so no unstated weighted integrability of individual diagonal derivatives is required. Step 2.2 proves gradient p=p times score even at density zeros by Fermat, bounds the cross term by the two finite squared moments, and bounds the boundary term by C(1+E||psi||^2)/(2R). Steps 3.1–4.1 use the integrable divergence and cross term to remove cutoffs and obtain the sign-correct identity. Lebesgue-null changes are P_p-null; AC_omega covers the actual Lebesgue, Borel, representative, substitution and smoothing interfaces, with no full AC. d=1, density zeros, empty admissible parameter set, and R to infinity are covered. Hyvarinen Theorem 1/Appendix A imposes a pointwise boundary condition; this local cutoff proof independently proves the stated stronger boundary formulation. No diagram is required. Accepted reader repair verbatim; synchronized only the stale manifest dependency mirror."
