          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "compute-chain-derivative-correction",
          "claim": "By [F4] and step 2.1, the chain correction is $\\sum_{x\\in\\{0,1\\}}q'_{1,0}(x)\\log(q_{1,0}(x)/p_0(x))=\\frac18\\log\\frac32-\\frac18\\log\\frac12=\\frac18\\log3>0$. Subtracting it from the first two CD terms $-1/4$ gives $\\left.\\frac{d}{d\\theta}\\operatorname{CD}_1(\\theta)\\right|_{\\theta=0}=-\\frac14-\\frac18\\log3$, as stated. Thus the stop-gradient CD-1 direction also differs from the exact CD-1 objective derivative.",
          "step": "4.1",
