      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-59",
        "notes": "Read the complete Example, four verification steps, all eight direct prerequisites and the sole scoped TikZ diagram. For every finite theta, the positive logistic law normalizes; the half-identity plus half-refresh kernel is positive, stochastic, smooth and p-invariant, so all finite-state CD theorem hypotheses hold. At theta=0 recomputed p=(1/2,1/2), q1=(3/4,1/4), p1 derivative=-1/4, and q1 derivative=(1/8,-1/8). Energy derivative=(0,1) gives likelihood derivative=-1/2 and population stop-gradient=-1/4. The logarithmic correction is (log(3/2)-log(1/2))/8=log(3)/8>0, so scalar CD derivative=-1/4-log(3)/8. Checked theta=0 is an interior point; denominator 1+exp(-theta) never vanishes and no boundary parameter or infinity is included. The TikZ arrows run from source x to target y, with each loop labeled 3/4 and both cross-arrows 1/4, exactly the displayed matrix; proof is independent of the diagram. The witness asserts neither general bias sign nor asymptotic inconsistency. Example contains no hyperlinks before its complete references section; no repair or missing diagram."
